From 28bd5334629524a89e903027994ea9af8139b990 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Viet Hung Nguyen <hvn@calif.io>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 20:30:01 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat: Add TimeNanos logical type

Add a `time-nanos` logical type, backed by `long`, that mirrors the
existing `time-micros` type: the time of day as the number of
nanoseconds after midnight.

Changes:
- `Schema::TimeNanos` and `Value::TimeNanos(i64)`, with parsing of
  `{"type": "long", "logicalType": "time-nanos"}` and serialization
  back to the same JSON.
- Encode/decode as a zig-zag long, like `TimeMicros`.
- `Value::resolve` accepts `TimeNanos`, `Long`, or `Int`; a new
  `Details::GetTimeNanos` error covers the mismatch case.
- Serde support in the value deserializer and the schema-aware
  serializer.
- Schema compatibility: `long <-> time-nanos` promotion, same rules as
  `time-micros`.
- Schema equality, test helper schema examples, README and crate docs.
- Unit tests for each of the above.

Note: `time-nanos` is not part of the Avro specification. Other
implementations will treat it as an unknown logical type and fall back
to the underlying `long`, so data remains readable across
implementations.
